=== SURVEY ===
Source of truth surveyed:
  - Shared KMP SSE client (apps/shared/.../net/sse/): SseClient.subscribe() -> LiveSubscription(events: Flow<LiveEvent>,
    connection: StateFlow<Connection>). Connection = Connecting|Open|Reconnecting|Stale|Closed. Auto-reconnect (capped
    exp-backoff + jitter), resume via Last-Event-ID, staleness after freshnessWindowMillis (default 120_000 = ADR-013 2 min).
    KtorSseTransport reads tokenProvider.token() per open (reconnect carries the refreshed bearer). LiveSubscription ctor
    is internal -> Android wraps subscribe() behind a LiveFeed seam (public LiveStream) instead of constructing it.
  - Web live behaviour: useLiveConnection (SSE state -> connected/reconnecting/disconnected/unknown), useVehicleLive
    (merge vehicle_update state/signals, never drop known values), LiveStaleDataBanner (>2 min), LiveIndicator.
  - Existing Android A2 surfaces (reused, not duplicated): components/datadisplay/LiveIndicator.kt + LiveConnectionStatus
    + liveConnectionColor; components/feedback/Banners.kt LiveStaleDataBanner(onReconnect, staleForLabel).
  - Auth graph (A4): AuthSession.asTokenProvider(); AuthState SignedOut|Authenticating|SignedIn|Refreshing|Error.
  - Data graph (A5): DataContainer manual DI + viewModelFactory; BaseFeedViewModel (WhileSubscribed reshare +
    collectAsStateWithLifecycle bind); SelectedVehicleStore; DashboardViewModelTest virtual-time pattern.
  - ADRs: 002 native, 004 KMP core, 008 auth (SSE must re-auth), 009 foreground-only SSE + stale>2min, 010 gate triad,
    011 DoD, 013 offline/2-min stale, 015 a11y, 016 single redacting logger / PII redaction.
  - lifecycle-process was NOT in the version catalog -> added (ProcessLifecycleOwner needs it).

=== REASONING ===
Chosen approach (layered, ADR-009):
  - LiveFeed seam over the shared SseClient (LiveStream(events, connection)) so the store is testable without the
    internal LiveSubscription ctor, while production still uses the real client end-to-end.
  - LiveSessionStore (app-scoped, NOT a ViewModel): gates ONE subscription on (foreground && authenticated, epoch) via
    combine -> distinctUntilChanged -> flatMapLatest -> scan -> stateIn(WhileSubscribed). Folds Connection + LiveEvents
    into LiveSessionState (connection/staleness verbatim from the client; vehicle_update/signal_change merged per-vehicle;
    last-known retained). Three gates compose: app foreground (ProcessLifecycleOwner) AND authenticated AND a page
    observing (WhileSubscribed) -> stream open exactly when foreground live data is needed; any drop tears it down cleanly.
  - AppLifecycleSseBinder binds ProcessLifecycleOwner.lifecycle -> store.setForeground (foreground-only; testable via a
    LifecycleRegistry fake).
  - LiveViewModel projects status/isStale/lastMessage/active-vehicle + retry(); registered in DataContainer's factory.
  - LiveConnectionIndicator + LiveStaleBanner composables wire the VM to the A2 surfaces (localized labels, retry action).
  - Re-auth WITHOUT per-page token code: (1) transport reads token() per (re)open; (2) authenticated false->true reopens
    with the new credential; (3) reconnect()/retry() bumps epoch (fresh open) and nudges onReauth = session token().
Rejected: a 2nd SSE entry / duplicated Ktor transport in Android (DRY / ADR-004); modifying shared core (out of allowed
  files); per-page token handling (ADR-008/009 say centralised); hiding panels when stale (ADR-009/013 forbid).

